d 'IMPORTR': module to import R data files (.Rdata, .Rda, .Rds) into Stata over an R or Python bridge
d
d  .Rdata and .Rds files are compressed binary objects in R's own
d serialization format, so there is no pure-Stata way to read them;
d something outside Stata has to do the decoding. importr takes a
d dual-bridge approach so that it works on machines with R and on
d machines without it. It first tries R, converting the file
d through the haven package; if that does not produce a dataset it
d falls back to Stata's built-in Python integration, reading with
d pyreadr and writing with pyreadstat. Either path lands the data
d in memory, and the bridge that succeeded is reported. Handles
d .Rdata, .Rda, and .Rds. 
d
d KW: import; R; data management; interoperability
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f importr.ado
f importr.sthlp
f importr_example.rdata
f importr_example.rds
